{"ts":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z","author":"codex-root-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/666 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/667\\n\\nDuplicate check: all-status searches for run 30072359707, the exact Node 22 SQLite warning, workspace-memory Windows write failure, and workspace history unreadability found historical cross-platform items and the closed Bun release item pm-cedo0g, but no current owner for these exact nightly failures."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-lvd647"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-666/GH-667: nightly Node 22 stderr and Windows permission-contract regressions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Restore the supported nightly matrix by keeping optional SQLite diagnostics out of machine-readable stderr on Node 22 and making unwritable-memory/history tests assert capability outcomes rather than POSIX-only permission behavior on Windows."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","area:sdk","cross-platform","gh-issue","nightly","node22","windows"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-root-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Optional SQLite capability loading does not leak runtime experimental warnings into CLI/MCP machine channels; tests use scoped deterministic failure seams instead of global warning suppression or POSIX chmod assumptions; Node 22 and Windows focused regressions pass; no nightly job, assertion, or supported runtime is removed; GitHub issues #666 and #667 are linked and closed only after exact hosted proof."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"codex-root-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Inspect scheduled run 30072359707 at db1b7111: Node 22 fails three built-CLI/MCP tests because node:sqlite ExperimentalWarning pollutes stderr; Windows fails workspace-memory and drift-scan permission simulations because chmod does not make paths unreadable."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Supported Node and OS matrix tests observe clean machine-readable process channels and deterministic injected filesystem failure semantics; nightly validation passes without silencing unrelated warnings or skipping platform coverage."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Node 22 reports experimental SQLite warnings on stderr and Windows permission-based fixtures do not reproduce the intended failures, causing five tests and two nightly jobs to fail."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"cross-runtime SDK and nightly validation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":true},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Daily validation reports red after otherwise-correct SDK changes, obscuring real release risk and making structured CLI/MCP channels unreliable on Node 22."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-801d","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"},{"id":"pm-cedo0g","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"},{"id":"pm-hcrmye","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"},{"id":"pm-klo8","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z